WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:12.740
Welcome!

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.200
Hi!

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.400
So we're going to speak Norwegian ...

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.440
And you know this language, because you're half Norwegian.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:19.260
Yes.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.500
The job you do here ...

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:29.780
There were 9000 children who were considered for this job.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.660
But you weren't one of them?

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.460
No. Because I was sick.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.100
But my brother was there.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.040
And ...

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.280
So your brother wanted a part?

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:42.820
Yes.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.120
But ...

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.920
... after ...

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:53.600
... we had been on a summer vacation in Oslo ...

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.480
... HBO called my mother ...

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.820
... and said that they wanted to meet Alberto, my brother.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.740
And I came with him.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.180
And they liked me.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:09.820
And after a few weeks ...

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:12.500
I got the part, and he didn't.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.180
So you had just come with him?

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:16.960
Yes!

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:18.540
And they saw you there?

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:19.380
Mhm!

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:24.500
But what did you brother say?

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:28.020
Can you tell me?

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.560
Uhhh ... He ...

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.780
Did he become upset or turn sour?

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.060
Uh. He turned sour.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.340
He turned sour!

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:37.520
He was jealous of you!

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:38.020
Yes.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:39.780
But he's okay now?

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:40.680
Yes.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:45.600
Tell me, what did you have to learn to do this part?

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:48.280
I had to learn Neapolitan.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.740
Which ... You're Italian?

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:57.480
Yes. But I had to learn a Neapolitan dialect.

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:00.980
But ... Can we hear the difference between Italian and ...

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.020
Yes.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:04.860
In Norwegian, it's:

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:07.420
«Det du gjør, gjør jeg.»

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.260
In regular Italian, it's:

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.100
«Quello che fai tu, lo faccio io.»

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.680
And in Neapolitan, it's:

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.460
«Quello che fai tu, lo faccio io.»

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:25.240
Difficult!

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:26.480
You're so good!

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:31.360
I have a picture here, that I found from the filming.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:36.920
... Of you. It's a picture of you with a strange thing on your nose, what is this?

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:37.820
Yes.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:42.520
It's to heat the nose or your hands.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:46.180
Oh, so it's a heating pad? Aha.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:47.760
Why?

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.080
Because it was cold!

00:02:54.820 --> 00:03:03.580
And I remember one time that was difficult because it was minus 5 degrees celcius.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.700
And we were just wearing sandals and ...

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.900
So you were supposed to act like it was warm?

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:10.940
Yes.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.340
When it was minus degrees?

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:14.120
Yes.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:16.300
That wasn't easy?

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:19.500
But ...

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:23.900
Had you acted in anything before this, or ..?

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.040
No.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:29.100
This was the first.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:33.200
But tell me how ...

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:38.040
You receive a lot of praise, both in Norwegian and international press ...

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:42.380
I've read that you're extremely good at conveying emotions.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:46.440
Even when you're not talking, you're good at conveying emotions.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:51.080
And what would it look like, if you were to think about something sad right now?

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.440
You do look very sad!

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:01.560
The part you're playing is ...

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:06.700
The role you're playing is Elena, who is very timid.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:08.380
Are you timid yourself?

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:12.140
Timid?

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:14.000
Timid ... Are you shy?

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:14.860
Yes!

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:15.640
You are?

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:16.480
Yes.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:19.700
But when do you get shy, when are you the most shy?

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.320
Now, maybe.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.140
Now?!

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:26.420
A little!

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:29.240
But it's going well!

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:30.100
Yes!

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:31.480
Di you want to become an actress?

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.200
Yes.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:42.500
Elisa, you're going to celebrate Christmas in Norway.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:43.000
Yes.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:44.140
Are you looking forward to that?

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:44.840
Yes.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.980
Because there's snow there!

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.100
And my family.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:55.380
And my grandmother's meatballs.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.160
Meatballs?

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:56.940
Yes!

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:00.580
Thank you so much for being here, Elisa. Thank you!

